<title>POLAND: Polish ferry shipping rises in Jan-July.</title>
<headline>Polish ferry shipping rises in Jan-July.</headline>
<dateline>GDANSK, Poland 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of passengers, cars, buses and trucks using Polish ferry services rose in the January-July period, while the number of railway wagons carried on the services fell, Polish ferry operators said on Monday.</p>
<p>The three ferry firms which ship to and from Polish ports are Polferries, belonging to Polska Zegluga Baltycka, Unity Line owned by Polska Zegluga Morska and Lian Ferry controlled by Sweden's Stena Line.</p>
